 https://leetcode.com/articles/get-highest-answer-rate-question/

Get the highest answer rate question from a table survey_log with these columns: uid, action, question_id, answer_id,
q_num, timestamp.

uid means user id; action has these kind of values: "show", "answer", "skip"; answer_id is not null when
action column is "answer",
while is null for "show" and "skip"; q_num is the numeral order of the question in current session.

Write a sql query to identify the question which has the highest answer rate.

Example:
Input:
+------+-----------+--------------+------------+-----------+------------+
| uid  | action    | question_id  | answer_id  | q_num     | timestamp  |
+------+-----------+--------------+------------+-----------+------------+
| 5    | show      | 285          | null       | 1         | 123        |
| 5    | answer    | 285          | 124124     | 1         | 124        |
| 5    | show      | 369          | null       | 2         | 125        |
| 5    | skip      | 369          | null       | 2         | 126        |
+------+-----------+--------------+------------+-----------+------------+
Output:
+-------------+
| survey_log  |
+-------------+
|    285      |
+-------------+
Explanation:
question 285 has answer rate 1/1, while question 369 has 0/1 answer rate, so output 285.
Note: The highest answer rate meaning is: answer number's ratio in show number in the same question.


Method 1


Select ques_id, SUM(case when action_id = ’answer’ then 1 else 0 end)/ SUM(case when action_id = ’show’ then 1 else 0 end) as answer_rate
Group by 1
Order by SUM(case when action_id = ’answer’ then 1 else 0 end)/ SUM(case when action_id = ’show’ then 1 else 0 end) DESC
LIMIT 1

Python

df_grouped1=df.loc[df[‘action_id’]==’show’,:].group_by(‘ques_id’, as_index=False).agg(impressions= (‘action_id’, ‘count’))
df_grouped2=df.loc[df[‘action_id’]==’answer’,:].group_by(‘ques_id’, as_index=False).agg(answers= (‘action_id’, ‘count’))

df_merged=df_grouped1.merge(df_grouped2, how =‘inner’, on=‘ques_id’)
df_merged[‘answer_rate’]=df_merged[‘answers’]/df_merged[‘impressions’]
df_merged=df_merged.sort_values(by=‘answer_rate’, ascending=False)

df_merged[‘ques_id’][0]


